  "name": "GE C204 Gravity Distortion Time Displacement Unit (John Titor 2036 -> 1975)",
  "description": "FP64 CUDA 2D spatial simulation of the General Electric Army Model C204 Gravity Distortion Time Displacement Unit (TMIM-200S/4005, CompleteTitor, Pohlman US 2006/0073976 A1, & Tipler 1974). Evaluates the calibrated 3+1 ADM Effective Phenomenological Metric g_00^eff = -(alpha^2 - ||beta||^2) inside the Van Den Broeck 22m x 6m x 6m ellipsoidal loading envelope (5m mass offset, 8m rear, 11m forward, 170 deg aft X-ray venting cone) alongside the full onboard flight computer state machine (50/75/100% power, 126k/201.6k/288k C, 3.4/6.2/10 yrs/hr, 240s / 54k C VGL checks, Borda 3-computer voting, 1.5-2.0 G cabin gradient, 100-120 F hull temp, 1s rainbow/UV burst, optical blackout, and Automatic Origin Return).",
